# Styled selects (dashboard)

Never use a browser-native `<select>` / `<option>` in `apps/dashboard`.

Use the shared Radix select from `apps/dashboard/src/components/ui/select.tsx`:

- `Select`, `SelectTrigger`, `SelectValue`, `SelectContent`, `SelectItem`

## Do

```tsx
import { Select, SelectContent, SelectItem, SelectTrigger, SelectValue } from '../ui/select'

<Select value={value} onValueChange={setValue} disabled={disabled}>
  <SelectTrigger className="h-8 text-xs" aria-label={label}>
    <SelectValue />
  </SelectTrigger>
  <SelectContent>
    {options.map((opt) => (
      <SelectItem key={opt.value} value={opt.value}>
        {opt.label}
      </SelectItem>
    ))}
  </SelectContent>
</Select>
```

## Named things

A select or dropdown of agents, people, teams, flows, projects, tags,
calendars, channels, or connections uses `ChoiceSelect` (or `ChoiceOption`
inside a `DropdownMenuItem`). `AgentSelect` is the agent-only wrapper.
The row is mark then name: avatar, brand logo, workflow, folder, or `#`.

Enums (mode, language, cadence, a count) stay a plain `Select` with text.

```tsx
import { ChoiceSelect } from '../ui/ChoiceSelect'

<ChoiceSelect
  aria-label={label}
  value={value}
  onValueChange={setValue}
  groups={[
    {
      items: agents.map((agent) => ({
        value: agent.id,
        label: agent.name,
        kind: 'agent',
        agent,
      })),
    },
  ]}
/>
```

## Do not

- `<select className=...><option>...`
- One-off custom dropdowns that reimplement the same pattern
- Leaving native selects when touching a file — convert them in the same change

Exceptions: none for product UI. Tests may assert on the styled control via roles/labels.
